    "created_at": "2026-06-26T10:54:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-26T10:54:03Z",
    "body": "From a Service Worker perspective, this is an understandable change to prevent XS-Leaks. However, I believe this behavior can be highly confusing to web developers because they generally assume that subresource requests will be intercepted by Service Workers by default.\n\nThe existing skip cases, such as the \"serviceworker\" script itself or the \"webidentity\" destination, are easy to justify for infinite loop prevention and user privacy. Bypassing the Service Worker for XS-Leak prevention on same-origin/cross-origin media requests, however, can feel very counterintuitive. We will need to thoroughly explain the 'why' and the 'what' to the developer community, especially the requirement to explicitly use the crossorigin attribute to enable Service Worker interception.\n\nCCing @monica-ch to heads up as the other Service Worker spec editor.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
